All ten gate-ir dev programs are reused. Three additional scalar units cover each export,
signed/unsigned widths, arithmetic wrap/overflow, compare/div/rem/right-shift signedness,
casts, boolean logic, nested calls, six arguments, void calls, loops, break and traps.
Native drivers write full 64-bit result patterns; wasm results are compared against these
bytes, never merely an exit-status byte. Native trap code statuses are pinned in cases.tsv;
wasm traps are checked as WebAssembly.RuntimeError (MVP does not expose Omega trap numbers).
Two translations of every unit were byte-identical.

